WEBVTT

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.590
Typhoon number eight in the Carolines has developed into an extra powerful type.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.330
With the center wind velocity.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.720
...registering 60 meters per second and a maximum at more than 80 meters.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.240
It is moving north.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:18.210
and approaching the Japanese mainland at a speed of 50 kilometers an hour.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.440
Attention all stations here.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.340
The shipping association has just announced that the gennyomaru of the Machu Bishi steamship company

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.620
It's somewhere near the center of the typhoon.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.520
Stand by for distress signals.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.950
He was on charge.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.470
Twelve degrees north, east of Beirut.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:55.390
What's that?

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:56.550
Off Beirut?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.500
Are you sure?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:58.740
Yes, sir.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:02:59.960
Directly east of Beirut.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:13.150
the island right near the blast area sir we're in the atomic test area captain we've hit the reef

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.740
we're on ground are you all right

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.540
They're flying around this radioactive area.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.030
Look at the fuel gauge. It's low.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.920
JA7426 calling. Gas.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.180
I'm returning to ship.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.230
In any case, the search looks hopeless.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.450
By now, we surely should have seen something.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:42.780
Four men there.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.600
This helicopter calling urgent, calling Satsuma.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:48.290
Come in.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.120
Survivors sighted on beach and cape.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.310
Going down now to attempt to pick up.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.480
Will we get a chance for an interview?

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.920
At least let us in. Let us get some pictures of the men.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.320
Rhea, what's the big secret?

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.750
Dr. Harada. Good morning, Doctor.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.010
Here's the examination records of the men.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:57.190
It's astounding. Look at this. I can't understand it.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:00.950
Sit there, please.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.030
Tell me, how do you men feel?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:19.210
I mean to say, are you feeling all right?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.240
Is anything troubling any of you now?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.800
Do they understand me?

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:24.640
Yes, sir.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:25.910
They understand you, I mean.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:27.440
Sir?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.260
Yes, yes.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.480
I feel hungry all the time here because I used to eat all I wanted on the ship, huh?

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:36.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.550
What's this?

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.410
I'm from the Nito Press.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.920
Nito Press? Weren't you told no pictures would be permitted? Give me the film.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:47.510
John.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:54.470
Buddha, I'm a journalist.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.800
It's highly irregular. There's danger of radiation.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.520
They're all normal though, aren't they?

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.160
Will you accept my card?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.310
My card, sir?

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.860
Since you're here now, I guess I can't throw you out.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.470
Better not. He's a bulldog.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:09.360
Bulldog?

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.330
Well, you see, I never let go.

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:16.970
When I'm out trapping a story, I hang on.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:24.490
Seriously, you know, there are millions of our readers who are curious about these men.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.180
All right, we can release the story.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.870
You can begin with an interview, and I'll fill you in on scientific details.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:35.550
Thank you. I want to say first, you're very fortunate to have returned unharmed.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:41.830
You suffered no radiation damage from the atomic graveyard, yet you were in a highly radioactive area.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.350
I think it was the juice that must have protected the juice.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.140
What sort of juice? The natives made us all drink juice.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.400
Natives?

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:54.310
Juice.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:59.300
Just a minute. It's supposed to be deserted there.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.250
On the front page, the headline will read Mysterious Natives on Biru Island.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.000
Mysterious Natives on Biru Island.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:12.430
That's it. And don't forget to quote the ambassador.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.500
Gentlemen, the Rolissican government had made very sure...

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.540
...before these atomic tests were undertaken...

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.500
...that the island of Biru was virtually uninhabited.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.980
We're still not convinced that it is not. Fact remains...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.300
We cannot explain the presence of these natives on the island at this time.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:38.320
It's our hope in the very near future to clarify matters.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.130
Sir, do you think they'll send an expedition?

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.290
That would seem likely, but I have not yet received word to that effect from my government.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.050
I wonder if anyone's an authority on those islands.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.770
Yes, Dr. Chujo, if anyone.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:51.560
Chujo?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.580
Famous linguist, ethnologist. He was leader of the Polynesian expedition.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.320
Good. Try to get an interview.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.810
I set it up already and sent Michi to get the picture.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:05.600
Thank you.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.260
The picture you wanted.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:08.360
Get what you wanted?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.350
No, not quite.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:09.960
Oh, here.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:14.320
Great.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.960
Oh, that's what I'd call a masterpiece.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.960
He doesn't like pictures, he says.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:25.500
Sorry.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:29.030
This is our intention to embarrass or annoy you, Mr. Chucho.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.860
It's just that you're the only person qualified to give us any information.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.000
Tell us, what about this expedition, Mr. Tujo?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:35.470
Eh?

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.630
Ask the Relisican government.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.360
It's really in case you look snagged.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.340
We won't try that again.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.480
Put away your camera now.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.660
Suppose you just talk to us.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.300
Very well, but no pictures.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:07.810
What's wrong? A mouse!

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:09.870
I'm so sorry.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:13.580
Oi! Shinji! Shinji!

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.480
There it goes, under the couch!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:16.920
Get your mouse!

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:19.180
And don't let it get in here again!

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.300
Sorry! I was looking for her!

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:30.220
See?

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:31.690
When they're at her.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:37.570
Yes.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:37.930
Oh.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:16.550
little moss here little moss you very kind of you well let's discuss the island are you going there

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:24.350
the expedition has requested that i go you are definitely going yes yes i i am as an

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:29.640
ethnologist i'm the linguist this island should open a new area for your studies

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.410
Yes, I think I'll find it very interesting.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:40.190
All of these Polynesian islanders share a good deal in common,

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.240
in their language structure and in their basic culture.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:48.040
Does that mean that they are basically similar to the people of Tahiti or Hawaii?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.110
Well, you've heard the legend, I suppose,

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.330
that all these islands once formed a huge continent,

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.860
like the so-called Lost Atlantis.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.920
I see you don't believe that.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.260
I believe only what I can see through the lens.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:04.980
And whatever you should, eh?

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:09.110
To me, the camera shutter clicking is like the sound of the guillotine.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:10.270
Guillotine.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.570
Palers, that's right.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.480
Unlike the guillotine, you don't always know when your picture has been taken.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:20.420
This way, Doctor.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:27.730
Hello, Doctor.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:28.830
Hello, Doctor.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:29.820
Thank you.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:34.110
How do you do, Doctor? Good to see you, sir.

